hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"985","Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Abdul Aziz, meaning Al-Darawardi, told us, Zaid bin Aslam told us, Bishr bin Muadh told us, Abd told us Allah ibn Ja`far, Zayd ibn Aslam told me, H. Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, that Malik told him, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, H. Abu Musa narrated to us, a soul, Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, H. Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman narrated to us, And I read it to Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, on the authority of Al-Shafi’i, I am Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, and on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, and on the authority of Al-Araj they narrate it, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. H And Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Ibn Abi Hazim told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, H And Bundar told us, Muhammad, narrated to us Shu’bah, said: I heard Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Abu Musa, narrated to us. Muhammad bin Ja’far, narrated to me Shu’bah, narrated to me, on the authority of Suhail On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Muhammad ibn Abd al-A’la and Abu al-Ash’ath narrated to us, saying: Narrated to us Mu`tamar, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Ahmad bin Abdah narrated to us, Ziyad bin Abdullah Al-Qushayri narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, and Bundar told us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa’id, told us Abdullah bin Sa’id bin Abi Hind. He said: Abd al-Rahman al-Araj told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever performs a rak’ah of Fajr prayer before... “When the sun rises, he has attained it, and whoever performs one rak’ah of the afternoon prayer before the sun sets, he has attained it.” Abu Bakr said: The meaning of their hadiths is the same, and this is the hadith of Al-Darawardi, except that Abu Musa, in his hadith, said on the authority of Muhammad bin Jaafar: And who He performed two rak'ahs of the afternoon prayer"
